  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Causing an action",
   "texto": [
    "The causative presents someone as the one who makes another person or thing take action. Algunas formas frecuentes llevan **-이-, -히-, -리-, -기-, -우-, -구-** o **-추-**: 먹다 → **먹이다** (dar de comer), 입다 → **입히다** (vestir a alguien), 자다 → **재우다** (acostar a alguien), 웃다 → **웃기다** (hacer reír). There is no safe rule to choose the suffix: learn each verb with its causative form.",
    "아기에게 우유를 **먹여요** = doy leche al bebé."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Use and conjugation",
   "texto": [
    "Se conjugan como verbos normales: 먹이다 → **먹여요**, 입히다 → **입혀요**, 재우다 → **재워요**. Some forms coincide with passive: the meaning and arguments of the phrase allow them to be distinguished."
   ]
